		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Preparing Bullet 2.83 and 3.x at github, clone and test!]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=33473#p33473"><![CDATA[
The Bullet Physics SDK source code repository is now located at github: <a href="http://github.com/bulletphysics/bullet3" class="postlink">http://github.com/bulletphysics/bullet3</a><br>I am preparing an initial Bullet 2.83 version from that repo, please clone and test the code and discuss in this forum if there are serious issues.<br><br>You can clone using either git or subversion/svn:<br><br>git clone <a href="http://github.com/bulletphysics/bullet3" class="postlink">http://github.com/bulletphysics/bullet3</a><br>svn co <a href="http://github.com/bulletphysics/bullet3/trunk" class="postlink">http://github.com/bulletphysics/bullet3/trunk</a> bullet3<br><br>This year we are migrating toward Bullet 3.x. The Bullet 2.x API will be maintained during this year, while we are developing the Bullet 3.x API.<br>Thanks and enjoy!<br>Erwin<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=10522">bullet_team</a> — Sat May 17, 2014 10:12 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
